            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the remaining part of the land to her daughter Krishna and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of it to her son Bora. After giving them their shares, she keeps the remaining land for herself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.175,
            0.721,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) What part of the original land did Krishna get?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.199,
            0.69,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) What part of the original land did Bora get?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.223,
            0.823,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) What part of the original land did Somu keep for herself?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.251,
            0.701,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Find the area of a rectangle of sides 3 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ft and 9 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.29,
            0.849,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Tsewang plants four saplings in a row in his garden. The distance between two saplings is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " m. Find the distance between the first and last sapling. ["
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Draw a rough diagram with four saplings with distance between two saplings as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " m]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.402,
            0.664,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Which is heavier: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 2 } { 1 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of 500 grams or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{20}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of 4 kg?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.447,
            0.847,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is the Product Always Greater than the Numbers Multiplied?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.5,
            0.848,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since, we know that when a number is multiplied by 1, the product remains unchanged, we will look at multiplying pairs of numbers where neither of them is 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.556,
            0.847,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When we multiply two counting numbers greater than 1, say 3 and 5, the product is greater than both the numbers being multiplied."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.446,
            0.603,
            0.55,
            0.623
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "3 \\times 5 = 15"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.627,
            0.604,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The product, 15, is more than both 3 and 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.65,
            0.632,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "But what happens when we multiply "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and 8?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.454,
            0.689,
            0.543,
            0.723
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 } \\times 8 = 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.725,
            0.846,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the above multiplication the product, 2, is greater than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{4},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " but less than 8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.79,
            0.6,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What happens when we multiply "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.84,
            0.55,
            0.877
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\frac { 3 } { 4 } } \\times { \\frac { 2 } { 5 } } = { \\frac { 6 } { 2 0 } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.88,
            0.846,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us compare this product "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 6 } { 2 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " with the numbers "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 2 } { 5 } } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " For this,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.938,
            0.194,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "184"
            }
          ]
        },
